ck":false,"Summary":"Updated README.md platform documentation for NexusMobility Modern Clean Light Eco-Tech Platform.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# 🌿 NexusMobility — Modern Clean Light Eco-Tech Platform\n\n> An enterprise-ready, production-grade web application for intelligent urban transit, carpooling, and metropolitan carbon emissions reduction. Inspired by Apple Mobility and Tesla Sustainability interfaces, featuring a crisp, high-contrast light theme, interactive 4-seat visual car diagram, route compatibility matching engine, and zero computer science/academic data structure jargon.\n\n---\n\n## 🎨 Design System & Palette: Modern Clean Light Eco-Tech\n\n- **Primary Background**: Soft Slate Gray (`#F4F7F6`)\n- **Card Surface & Panels**: Pure White Glass (`#FFFFFF`) with subtle emerald border glows\n- **Sustainability Accent**: Urban Emerald Green (`#059669`) for active status, eco-badges, and CO₂ metrics\n- **Primary Action Accent**: Clean Electric Blue (`#2563EB`) for route corridors, primary CTA buttons, and interactive maps\n- **Priority Standby Accent**: Energy Amber (`#D97706`) for priority lounge slots and warnings\n- **Dark Typography**: Deep Charcoal (`#0F172A`) for high-contrast, crisp readability\n- **Muted Typography**: Cool Slate (`#64748B`) for subtext and metadata\n\n---\n\n## 📁 Package Architecture\n\n```text\nnexusmobility/\n├── index.html        # Clean light dashboard UI, 4-seat car blueprint & eco-receipt modal\n├── styles.css        # Modern eco-tech light design system & 3D tilt physics\n├── app.js            # Light 3D canvas map, route compatibility engine & state manager\n└── README.md         # Full operating manual & platform guide\n```\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ How to Operate the Application\n\n### 1. Direct Browser Launch\n- Simply double-click [index.html](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html) or open it in any modern browser (Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Brave, Mozilla Firefox).\n- No external server or build tools required.\n\n### 2. Export Entire Project as .ZIP\n- In the top navigation bar, click the **\"Export Package\"** button.\n- The built-in exporter packages `index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`, and `README.md` into `nexusmobility-eco-tech-platform.zip` and triggers an immediate download.\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 Feature & Module Operation Guide\n\n### 1. 🚀 One-Click \"Rush-Hour Simulation\"\n- Click **\"Rush-Hour Simulation\"** in the top navigation bar.\n- Instantly populates the system with registered driver partners, pending commuter requests, a passenger in the priority standby lounge, and an active dispatched shared trip with live carbon offset calculations and a `96% Route Match` badge.\n\n### 2. 🗺️ Metropolitan Eco-Route Finder & 3D Spatial Map (Light Blueprint)\n- **3D Spatial Navigation**: Click and hold anywhere on the map to orbit the 3D metropolitan corridor; use the mouse scroll wheel to zoom.\n- **Station Telemetry**: Hover over any hub (e.g. *Tech Park Alpha*, *Central Financial Core*, *Bayfront Terminal*) to view elevation and transit zones.\n- **Route Calculation**:\n  1. Select an **Origin Station** and a **Destination Station** (or click the swap button `⇄`).\n  2. Click **\"Calculate Eco-Route\"**.\n  3. The electric-blue transit corridor illuminates in 3D, and the impact strip displays **Distance (km)**, **Estimated Time (min)**, **CO₂ Emissions Saved (kg)**, and **Pooled Fare ($)**.\n\n### 3. 👥 Passenger Dispatch Hub & Priority Standby Lounge\n- **Submit Ride Request**:\n  1. Enter commuter name (or leave empty for an auto-generated profile).\n  2. Choose pickup and drop stations, then click **\"Request Ride\"**.\n  3. The request enters the **Live Passenger Dispatch Pipeline** with priority tags.\n- **Priority Standby Lounge (Max 5 Slots)**:\n  - During peak demand periods, click **\"Add to Standby\"** to place passengers into the glowing 5-slot circular visual standby hub.\n  - The central hub tracks usage in real time (`0/5` to `5/5`) with automatic capacity limits.\n  - Click **\"Seat Commuter\"** to admit the front passenger once capacity opens.\n\n### 4. 🚗 Driver Partner Fleet & Interactive 4-Seat Car Diagram\n- **Interactive Visual Seat Selector**:\n  - In the driver onboarding form, click any passenger seat (`FRONT`, `REAR L`, `REAR R`) in the top-down car blueprint to toggle its availability between **Active (Green)** and **Reserved/Off**.\n  - The button dynamically tracks the seat count (e.g., `Onboard Partner (3 Seats)`).\n- **Flexible Identity & Booking Verification**:\n  - Enter a Driver Partner ID (e.g., `#101`) or a Booking Reference (e.g., `NX-501` or `BK-201`) in the lookup box and click **\"Verify Record\"**.\n  - Instantly verifies operational credentials, assigned station, route match score, and available seats.\n\n### 5. 🚖 Active Shared Trips & Route Compatibility Engine\n- **Dispatch Compatible Trip**:\n  - Click **\"Dispatch Next Compatible Trip\"**.\n  - Matches the next waiting commuter with an available driver partner who has free seats, displaying an eco-match score (e.g. `94% Route Match`).\n  - Decrements the partner's available seat capacity and adds the trip to the **Active Shared Trips** console.\n- **Eco-Receipt Generator**:\n  - Click **\"Eco-Receipt\"** on any active shared trip card to open the **Official Eco-Transit Journey Receipt** modal detailing carbon offset, distance, travel time, and fare breakdown with a 1-click **Print Receipt** option.\n- **Revert Last Confirmation (\"Instant Trip Reversal\")**:\n  - Click **\"Revert Last Confirmation\"**.\n  - Safely rolls back the most recent trip confirmation, restores driver seat availability, and returns the commuter back to the front of the dispatch queue.\n\n### 6. 🌱 Metropolitan Sustainability & Carbon Offset Analytics\n- Real-time impact indicators:\n  - **Net Atmospheric Carbon Reduction (kg CO₂)**\n  - **Collective Pooled Distance Traveled (km)**\n  - **Corridor Fleet Seat Utilization Rate (%)**\n  - **Top Eco-Driver Partners Leaderboard** with mileage records and star ratings.\n\n### 7. 🧲 3D Anti-Gravity Hover Tilt Physics\n- Move your mouse over any metric card, control panel, or transit widget.\n- Notice the subtle, elegant 3D tilt perspective along the cursor vector (`perspective(1000px) rotateX(...) rotateY(...) translateZ(10px)`) with dynamic elevation and soft responsive drop-shadow lighting.\n","Description":"Updated README.md for NexusMobility Modern Clean Light Eco-Tech Platform","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Kartik Bhosle\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a\\README.md","toolAction":"Writing file","toolSummary":"Update README.md for NexusMobility"}}]}
